From d07a21acd559242107c048cf0fd3846f456c339e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:00:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ptm: Play history for the Activity Log, GetStepHistoryAll

The Activity Log showed an empty Software Library: PTM kept no play history.

- Play history in /PlayHistory.dat in the PTM system save data (0x00010022), in the
  console's layout (https://www.3dbrew.org/wiki/PTM_Savegame): 0xC-byte entries with
  the title ID and an event (launch/close, applet/application) plus minutes since
  2000. The title that runs is logged as launched when emulation starts (also when
  the HOME Menu starts a title, which restarts emulation) and as closed when it stops.
  A file from a console (ring buffer) is read and kept, oldest entry first.
- GetPlayHistory returns the entries, GetPlayHistoryLength their number.
- GetStepHistoryAll (0x000F, Activity Log) answers with zeroed buffers and no entries;
  its layout is not documented.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
